    { "id": "O3", "text": "The health audit names what is stale by content and what is ambiguous, once per cause." }
  ],
  "stories": [
    { "id": "S1", "kind": "lifecycle", "text": "PreCompact tells the session to write JOURNAL/<NNNN>-<session>.md with links and attaches the health audit; SessionStart source compact says to read the plan, the newest JOURNAL and HEALTH entry first. Variations: V1 two sessions on one dossier (success: serial numbers without a gap or a collision); V2 no active dossier (success: no instruction); V3 Codex payload (as its recorded fixture shows).", "objectives": ["O1"],
      "tests": ["test:crates/legionctl/tests/e2e.rs::a_compaction_asks_for_a_journal_entry_and_the_next_start_reads_it_first"] },
    { "id": "S2", "kind": "requirement", "text": "An artifact with immutable: true (JOURNAL and HEALTH by default) refuses dossier write, edit and append; a superseding entry links the old one. Variations: V1 edit through a symlink or an outside editor (failure: dossier check reports the changed hash); V2 a new entry with supersedes (success).", "objectives": ["O2"],
      "tests": ["test:crates/legionctl/tests/e2e.rs::an_immutable_entry_refuses_each_write_and_a_correction_supersedes_it"] },
    { "id": "S3", "kind": "data-flow", "text": "dossier health counts a whole-file reference once as unanchored, marks anchored references stale only when their entity's hash changed, and names ambiguity (rows that disagree, a status git contradicts, a decision with no source) in an immutable HEALTH entry. Variations: V1 an unrelated edit of a referenced file (success: no stale finding for the anchored reference); V2 duplicate row ids (failure: named once).", "objectives": ["O3"],
      "tests": ["test:crates/legionctl/tests/e2e.rs::dossier_health_reports_content_anchored_staleness_and_ambiguity_once_per_cause"] }
  ],
